    "# GNN-Based Indian Sector Movement Prediction — Fixed & Reproducible Version\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is a corrected, self-contained version of the original GNN experiment.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Main corrections**\n",
    "- No hard-coded `/content/master_with_target.csv` dependency.\n",
    "- Builds the modelling table from the uploaded market, macro, and GDELT CSV files.\n",
    "- Uses **next-trading-day movement** as the target, so today's features are not used to predict today's label.\n",
    "- Chronological train/validation/test split.\n",
    "- Final models are trained on train+validation **without validating on data already used for fitting**.\n",
    "- Handles missing values and AUC edge cases.\n",
    "- Uses a dependency-free PyTorch implementation of GCN, GraphSAGE, GAT and an HGT-style heterogeneous attention model, so the notebook can run without `torch_geometric`.\n",
    "- Adds the requested figures at logical positions: network graph, training curves, per-sector AUC, model comparison, feature importance, and edge-importance heatmap.\n",
    "\n",
    "> Research note: the explanation plots use gradient-based saliency/edge importance rather than claiming to be the PyG `GNNExplainer` implementation."
   ]
  },
